+// subscriptions and bindings at once; with 50 entries the queue overflowed,
+// WebsocketWrite failed and the whole SHIP connection was torn down
+// ("kDataExchange: data exchange failed"). Entries only hold a pointer, the
+// payload is allocated per queued message, so a larger queue costs nothing
+// while idle.
+static const size_t kWriteQueueSize  = 1024;
